# --latest. Each line is: name version
# Each version is a published release with an archive for all four targets.
# scripts/release-pin-check.sh asks GitHub for those archives.
# .github/sibling-pin is the list of commits CI builds for the tests. The
# two lists name the same tool at the same point in its history:
# Each version is the release whose tag commit sibling-pin names, so the
# tests and the install run the same vissue 0.25.1, claimdag 0.9.1 and
# deedar 0.7.1.
vissue 0.25.1
claimdag 0.9.1
deedar 0.7.1
